    19	The use of functional constructs in programming languages such as
    20	Python has been advocated to help write more concise source code,
    21	improve parallelization, and reduce side effects. Nevertheless, their
    22	usage could lead to understandability issues. This paper reports
    23	the results of a controlled experiment conducted with 209 developers to assess the understandability of given Pythonic functional
    24	constructs—namely lambdas, comprehensions, and map/reduce/filter functions—if compared to their procedural alternatives. To
    25	address the study’s goal, we asked developers to modify code using functional constructs or not, to compare the understandability
    26	of different implementations, and to provide insights about when
    27	and where it is preferable to use such functional constructs. Results of the study indicate that code snippets with lambdas are
    28	more straightforward to modify than the procedural alternatives.
    29	However, this is not the case for comprehension. Regarding the
    30	perceived understandability, code snippets relying on procedural
    31	implementations are considered more readable than their functional
