    85	
    86	
    87	Widely-used programming languages have been conceived to be
    88	used by following either the imperative or object-oriented paradigm,
    89	_e.g.,_ C or Java. Some of these programming languages have also
    90	adopted constructs inspired by functional programming. This is the
    91	case of Java with the introduction of lambda functions in Java 1.8,
    92	Javascript with the introduction of higher-order functions, and,
    93	last but not least, Python. Such languages are not intrinsically
    94	functional (like Haskell or Scala), but give developers the flexibility
    95	to use functional constructs.
    96	
    97	Functional constructs have been advocated to help parallelization, avoiding the introduction of side effects in the source code [ 12,
    98	41 ]. At the same time, the understandability of such constructs
    99	has been questioned and discussed in previous studies and gray
